# Testing http requests with Visual Studio Code REST Client extension

## First random tests

### Palvelimen juuri
GET http://localhost:3000

### morotesti
GET http://localhost:3000/moro

### morotesti POST
POST http://localhost:3000/api/moro
content-type: application/json

{
  "sender": "Mei",
  "message": "testitervehdys"
}

## Items (test resource/endpoints using hard-coded mock data)

### get all items
GET http://localhost:3000/api/items

### get item by id
GET http://localhost:3000/api/items/3

### post a new item
POST http://localhost:3000/api/items
content-type: application/json

{
  "name": "Sitruuna"
}

### modify an existing item (by using item's id as a parameter in url)
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/items/3
content-type: application/json

{
  "name": "Päärynä"
}

### delete an item (by id)
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/items/2

## Users resource endpoints

### get all users
GET http://localhost:3000/api/users

### get user by id
GET http://localhost:3000/api/users/1

### add user
POST http://localhost:3000/api/users
content-type: application/json

{
  "username": "Uusi käyttäjä",
  "password": "salakala",
  "email": "newuser@example.com"
}

### update user
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/users/1
content-type: application/json

{
  "email": "john.doe@example.com"
}

### delete user
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/users/2

### user login
POST http://localhost:3000/api/users/login
content-type: application/json

{
  "username": "Uusi käyttäjä",
  "password": "salakala"
}

### get all entries
GET http://localhost:3000/api/entries

### get diary entry by id
GET http://localhost:3000/api/entries/1

### put diary entry by id
PUT http://localhost:3000/api/entries/3
content-type: application/json

{
  "mood": "happy"
}

### delete diary entry by id
DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/entries/2
